      "source_excerpt": "Each pigment can absorb different wavelengths of light, which allows the plant to absorb any light that passes through the taller trees. (credit: Jason Hollinger) How Light-Dependent Reactions Work The overall purpose of the light-dependent reactions is to convert light energy into chemical energy.",
      "source_dialog_text": "Sources\n\nSource passages linked to this claim.\n\nSource 1\nSource 2\nSource 3\nSOURCE PASSAGE\nConcepts of Biology\n\nChapter 5 Photosynthesis / 5.2 The Light-Dependent Reactions of Photosynthesis · PDF physical pages 138\n\nHighlighted text is linked to the selected claim.\n\nEach pigment can absorb different wavelengths of light, which allows the plant to absorb any light that passes through the taller trees. (credit: Jason Hollinger) How Light-Dependent Reactions Work The overall purpose of the light-dependent reactions is to convert light energy into chemical energy.\n\nThe complete source may reveal the answer to this problem.\n\nShow complete source\n\nOpenStax / Rice University · Access for free at openstax.org\n\nView original source\nSource record\nExact source positions\n\nSupport assessment: model check. Independent review is separate.\n\nModel support check",
